    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0343" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 111.70H81</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassadors in Great
                        Britain, France, Germany, Austria-Hungary, Italy, and Russia </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 22, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Colonel E. M. House, accompanied by Mrs. House, will sail for Europe December
                    28, S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Rotterdam.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>He proceeds at the request of the President and Secretary of State for the
                    purpose of taking information to our ambassadors in order that they may have a
                    more intimate knowledge of this Government’s attitude regarding certain phases
                    of international questions and in order to obtain from them their point of view
                    on these matters.</p>
                <p>Please impress on Foreign Office that Colonel House is not on a peace
                    mission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
